{
  "dom_id": "step-q339133",
  "name": "Question 5",
  "problem": "Evaluate the following limit:\n\n${lim}_{x\\to \\,{1}^{-}}\\frac{25\\operatorname{arccos}⁡(x)}{{x}^{2}+\\pi }=$\n{{field-1}}",
  "worked_solution": "Let's sketch the graph of $y=\\operatorname{arccos}⁡(x):$\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/multivariable/14189988/assets/85a182aabfe64c27eaafde94e3bdbede9409b02cfd87395cb2fc5543b09c4e05.png)\n\nThe domain of $\\operatorname{arccos}⁡(x)$ is $x\\in [-1,1].$  \n\nNow, substituting $x=1$ directly into the limit, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{lim}_{x\\to \\,{1}^{-}}\\frac{25\\operatorname{arccos}⁡(x)}{{x}^{2}+\\pi } & =\\frac{25\\operatorname{arccos}⁡(1)}{{1}^{2}+\\pi } \\\\  & =\\frac{25\\cdot 0}{1+\\pi } \\\\  & =0.\\end{aligned}\n$$",
  "calculator_instructions": "",
